{
  "language": "python",
  "case": "instance_calls",
  "why": "B35 (SSPN-48): calls through a variable whose type the code itself declares \u2014 an annotated parameter (plain, Optional, X | None), a local assigned once from a constructor, a `self.attr` typed by a class annotation, a constructor or a typed parameter, an inherited `self.m()`, an inherited classmethod on a class name, a Protocol, multiple inheritance. And the shapes that must be refused: a decoy class sharing the method name, a two-class union, a name bound to two types, an external type, an external base. B53 adds decoys for every refusal rule the #501 review added (app/decoys.py) and records the shapes left out on purpose \u2014 `super().m()`, `cls.m()`, `cls()` (app/gaps.py).",
